    {
      "item": "Amendment to IAS 1, Presentation of items of other comprehensive income (OCI) The amendment requires entities to separate items presented in OCI into two groups, based on whether or not they may be recycled to income statement in the future. Items that will not be recycled such as revaluation gains on property, plant and equipment will be presented separately from items that may be recycled in the future, such as deferred gains and losses on cash flow hedges. 1-July-2012",
